diepxuan (5.8.5+ppa~1) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(addr): `utils.addr._ip_locals()` now also excludes the RFC1918
    `172.16.0.0/12` range (used by Docker bridges and other local-only
    networks) in addition to `127.0.0.0/8` loopback. Previously, IPs like
    `172.17.0.1` (Docker default bridge) or `172.18.0.1` (user-defined
    bridge, e.g. `openclaw.diepxuan.corp`) were pushed to the internal
    DNS API as A records for the VM hostname, making the VM unreachable
    from any host except the one owning the bridge.
    - Behaviour is now pinned by `tests/unit/test_addr.py`.
    - VM sync (`vm:sync`) keeps working unchanged because it reads from
      `_ip_locals()`; no DNS API call surface change.

